flowchart TD
    %% Sources: brainstorm/00_context.md Scope, A-017, A-021, A-114, A-116, A-118,
    %% prompt-registry.lock.yml and access-control.lock.yml.

    start([Start: member needs a named prompt])
    registry[Open permission-filtered Registry]
    query[Search title or body; filter owner, status, access, and tags]
    results{Visible match found?}
    no_results[No Results]
    select[Select prompt property]
    detail[Prompt Property Detail]
    trusted{Approved trusted revision available?}
    unavailable[No Trusted Revision State]
    trusted_detail[Trusted Revision Detail with owner, status, revision ID, and model name]
    end_found([End: trusted revision identified])
    register_handoff([Continue to 02 Register Prompt])

    start --> registry
    registry --> query
    query --> results
    results -->|No| no_results
    no_results -->|Refine query| query
    no_results -->|Register a different prompt| register_handoff
    results -->|Yes| select
    select --> detail
    detail --> trusted
    trusted -->|No| unavailable
    unavailable -->|Return to Registry| query
    trusted -->|Yes| trusted_detail
    trusted_detail --> end_found

    %% Inaccessible prompt properties are returned as not found and never appear in Registry results.
    %% Semantic search and similar-prompt clustering are out of scope.
